    "done_when": "tests/test_producer_registration_survives_unlink.py, in a temporary RECKON_HOME, starts a producer, deletes its registration file under it, and shows the producer recreating the file at the same path, naming its pid, by its next wake-up. crew unwatch then finds and stops that producer rather than answering nothing-to-stop. The producer-holds-a-lease node (merge 320061aff) put the lease in a separate registration file written by update_watch_registration, and the seat record keeps its inode lock, so the node states which file unwatch reads the pid from. The declared negative control is executed and logged: with the recreation removed, unwatch answers nothing-to-stop and the test fails. Base and head arms of tests/test_producer_holds_a_lease.py, tests/test_producer_*.py and tests/test_crew_watch_lifetime.py show zero added failures.",
